\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The figure depicts an disk referring to the equilibrium measure when $r_0 = 0$. As the complex plane integral is reduced to a line integral, we draw the domain change and the point of interest $r_\tau $ where $V$ has a critical point. Around this point we depict the region around the minima, which in the method that should account for the main order of the integral we solve for. The left image corresponds to the case when $r_{j/N} >> N^{-\epsilon }$ and the right image corresponds to $r_{j/N} << N^{-\epsilon }$. In this case $r*_{\tau }$ will define the contributing region to the integral.}}{46}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
